{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 (v4.35.0) + Mathlib formalization establishing exact values of the balanced-sequence repetition threshold RTB(d) for alphabets of size 7, 9, and 10: RTB(7) = RTB*(7) = 6/5 < 5/4, RTB(9) = RTB*(9) = 8/7 < 7/6, and RTB(10) = RTB*(10) = 9/8 < 8/7, refuting three of the six values (d - 2)/(d - 3) listed as established for 5 <= d <= 10 in papers from 2018 to 2023. Each infimum is proved both from below via an exhaustive finite prefix-refutation witness tree checked by kernel reduction (905, 2941, and 4868 nodes respectively) and from above via an explicit 1-balanced Sturmian-colouring witness (v7, v9, v10) using all d letters and attaining its critical exponent as a maximum over minimal-period factors. Main results in the companion paper: 6 of 6 in Lean 4 (100%) · 12 of 12 abstract claims in Lean 4 (100%) · 18 of 18 paper claims in Lean 4 (100%) · 0 by external certificate · 0 by written proof. Within BalancedRepetitionThreshold, 11 of 13 Lean files import Mathlib; all 26 compared theorems in Solution.lean and all 193 public theorems in BalancedRepetitionThreshold compile with zero sorry, zero native_decide, and Lean's standard axioms only. The cases d = 5, 6, 8, and d >= 11 are not addressed. Companion working paper and verification archives are hosted at https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/balanced-sequences-critical-exponent.",
